    "injection": {
      "word": "INJECTION",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "The act of injecting or throwing in; -- applied particularly to the forcible throwing in of a liquid, or aëriform body, by means of a syringe, pump, etc.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "That which is injected; especially, a liquid medicine thrown into a cavity of the body by a syringe or pipe; a clyster; an enema. Mayne.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Anat.) (a) The act or process of filling vessels, cavities, or tissues with a fluid or other substance. (b) A specimen prepared by injection.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Steam Eng.) (a) The act of throwing cold water into a condenser to produce a vacuum. (b) The cold water thrown into a condenser. Injection cock, or Injection valve (Steam Eng.), the cock or valve through which cold water is admitted into a condenser. the condenser of a steam engine.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
